<title>COLOMBIA: Colombia's January oil output up 8.03 percent.</title>
<headline>Colombia's January oil output up 8.03 percent.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colombia's oil output rose to 639,000 barrels per day (bpd) in January, an 8.03 percent increase over the 591,497 bpd produced during the same month last year, according to the state oil company Ecopetrol.</p>
<p>The daily production figure was up only slightly over December 1996, however, when output was reported at 634,605 barrels.</p>
<p>Ecopetrol announced earlier this month that it expects to increase its oil exports by about 36 percent to 200,000 barrels per day in 1997. Its exports currently average about 147,200 barrels per day.</p>
<p>((-- Javier Mozzo, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944))</p>
